.SH NAME
hed\-scratch \- An ephemeral, unnamed buffer always one command away.
Useful for quick notes, paste\-and\-edit, or any throwaway text you
don\[cq]t want to commit to a file.
.PP
An ephemeral, unnamed buffer always one command away.
Useful for quick notes, paste\-and\-edit, or any throwaway text you
don\[cq]t want to commit to a file.
.SH Usage
.IP
.EX
:scratch
.EE
.PP
Opens the shared \f[CR][scratch]\f[R] buffer in a vertical split.
If the buffer is already shown in some window, focuses it instead of
creating a second split.
.PP
The buffer is kept non\-dirty so \f[CR]:q\f[R] from inside it just
closes the split.
Contents persist for the lifetime of the editor session \[em] if you
open \f[CR]:scratch\f[R] again later, you find the same text.
.SH Default leader binding
\f[CR]<space>z\f[R] is mapped to \f[CR]:scratch\f[R] in the default
\f[CR]src/config.c\f[R].
.SH Limitations
.IP \[bu] 2
One scratch buffer per session.
Open a regular \f[CR]:e file\f[R] if you want more than one.
.IP \[bu] 2
Contents are lost on quit \[em] by design.
Save with \f[CR]:w <path>\f[R] if you want to keep them.
.IP \[bu] 2
The buffer has no filename, so syntax highlighting and formatting
default to plain text.
